But let me caveat that, because I stated it too cleanly. "Volume" here is bundled — it could be more transactions per store, or more stores. With 200 locations, if they opened units over two years, part of that 15% is footprint, not same-store traffic. Those have very different implications: new stores carry build-out and depreciation, and might explain the two points of overhead creep.

Second caveat: mix. Even with flat menu prices, average ticket can rise if customers shift toward pricier drinks or food. So revenue could grow without unit volume growing.

